Ladybird decides isIntersecting from what is left of the target after
its ancestors’ clips and the root bounds, edge-inclusively. Gecko’s
DOMIntersectionObserver does the same: It intersects the rect with
each clip by EdgeInclusiveIntersection(), and isIntersecting is whether
a rect is left (IntersectionOutput::Intersects()). Blink’s
IntersectionGeometry clips the rect with VisualRectFlag::kEdgeInclusive
set. And WebKit’s IntersectionObserver::computeIntersectionState()
takes isIntersecting from edgeInclusiveIntersect() on the clipped rect.
